As @rdblue pointed out above, the sequences are actually valid for some storage implementations.  For example, S3 will allow a key with `..`, but it doesn't treat it as navigation, but rather as part of the key sequence.

The intent here is to not support usage of character sequences for the purposes of file system handling or navigation that some file systems support.  It's a little hard to explicitly enforce this.

