BasePartitionStatistics#internalSet has a null check
if (value == null)
{ return; }
this skips null values. I think this exists to prevent NPE from unboxing required premitive fields. But it means we cannot reset total_record_count back to null on objects that already have a non-null value from a previous stats computation. Fresh BasePartitionStatistics objects start with totalRecordCount = null by default, so we copy all fields and only set total_record_count when it's computable.

